<script setup lang="ts">import{computed,ref}from'vue';const name=ref('Ada'),rank=ref(2),fullscreen=ref(false),spotlight=ref(false);let timer:ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>|undefined;const conditions=computed(()=>[name.value.trim()?'LOWER(p.name) LIKE LOWER(:name)':'',rank.value?'p.rank >= :rank':''].filter(Boolean));const dql=computed(()=>`SELECT p FROM Person p${conditions.value.length?` WHERE ${conditions.value.join(' AND ')}`:''}`);const parameters=computed(()=>[name.value.trim()?`name = "%${name.value.trim()}%"`:'',rank.value?`rank = ${rank.value}`:''].filter(Boolean).join(' · ')||'none');const people=[{name:'Ada Lovelace',rank:3},{name:'Grace Hopper',rank:5},{name:'Alan Turing',rank:2},{name:'Barbara Liskov',rank:4}];const results=computed(()=>people.filter(p=>(!name.value.trim()||p.name.toLowerCase().includes(name.value.trim().toLowerCase()))&&(!rank.value||p.rank>=rank.value)));function animate(){spotlight.value=false;requestAnimationFrame(()=>{spotlight.value=true;clearTimeout(timer);timer=setTimeout(()=>spotlight.value=false,2100)})}</script><template><div :class="['filter-demo-modal',{'is-open':fullscreen}]" :role="fullscreen?'dialog':undefined" :aria-modal="fullscreen?'true':undefined"><section class="filter-demo" :class="{'is-spotlight':spotlight}"><header class="filter-demo__header"><div><p>THE FORM FILTER BUNDLE EFFECT</p><h2>Two filters. One line of controller code.</h2><span>Compare the boilerplate you maintain yourself with the work delegated to the bundle.</span></div><div class="filter-demo__controls"><button type="button" class="filter-demo__button filter-demo__button--primary" @click="animate">Show the magic</button><button type="button" class="filter-demo__button" @click="fullscreen=!fullscreen">{{fullscreen?'Close full screen':'Open full screen'}}</button></div></header><div class="filter-demo__comparison"><article class="filter-demo__side filter-demo__side--manual"><div class="filter-demo__badge">WITHOUT THE BUNDLE</div><h3>Your controller grows for every field</h3><pre><code><em>// name filter</em><br>if (&#36;name) {<br>  &#36;qb-&gt;andWhere(...);<br>  &#36;qb-&gt;setParameter(...);<br>}<br><br><em>// rank filter</em><br>if (&#36;rank) {<br>  &#36;qb-&gt;andWhere(...);<br>  &#36;qb-&gt;setParameter(...);<br>}</code></pre><small>Each filter means conditions, parameter names and repeated controller code.</small></article><div class="filter-demo__versus"><span>VS</span><i>same form</i></div><article class="filter-demo__side filter-demo__side--bundle"><div class="filter-demo__badge">WITH FORM FILTER BUNDLE</div><h3>Your controller delegates the translation</h3><pre><code>&#36;form-&gt;handleRequest(&#36;request);<br><br>&#36;queryBuilder = &#36;repository<br>  -&gt;createQueryBuilder('p');<br><br><span>&#36;filterBuilderUpdater<br>  -&gt;addFilterConditions(&#36;form, &#36;queryBuilder);</span></code></pre><small>Use normal Symfony filter types. The bundle adds only active conditions and bound parameters.</small></article></div><div class="filter-demo__workbench"><div class="filter-demo__form"><div class="filter-demo__section-title">1. The rendered Symfony form</div><label>Name contains<input v-model="name" type="search" placeholder="e.g. Ada" @input="animate"></label><label>Minimum rank<select v-model.number="rank" @change="animate"><option :value="0">Any rank</option><option :value="1">1+</option><option :value="2">2+</option><option :value="3">3+</option><option :value="4">4+</option><option :value="5">5</option></select></label></div><div class="filter-demo__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→<small>addFilterConditions()</small></div><div class="filter-demo__output"><div class="filter-demo__section-title">2. The query work generated for you</div><code class="filter-demo__dql">{{dql}}</code><small><b>Bound parameters:</b> {{parameters}}</small><div class="filter-demo__result"><b>{{results.length}} matching record{{results.length===1?'':'s'}}</b><span v-for="person in results" :key="person.name">{{person.name}} <i>Rank {{person.rank}}</i></span></div></div></div><footer class="filter-demo__footer"><strong>The win:</strong> add a third filter to the form, not another block of controller query code.</footer></section></div></template>
